fonts-nerd-symbols rebuilds Symbols Nerd Font from Nerd Fonts upstream source inputs.

Run from the repository root:

    ./debian/scripts/prepare-upstream 3.4.0+dfsg1

This sparse-clones the Nerd Fonts v3.4.0 source inputs needed for Symbols Only, removes Font Logos plus icon sets already packaged by Debian, and writes ../fonts-nerd-symbols_3.4.0+dfsg1.orig.tar.xz. Import it with:

    gbp import-orig --no-interactive --upstream-version 3.4.0+dfsg1 --pristine-tar ../fonts-nerd-symbols_3.4.0+dfsg1.orig.tar.xz

During package build, debian/scripts/build-clean-symbols generates the installed fonts from the shipped source inputs: it regenerates the Seti/custom source font from upstream SVGs, then runs font-patcher twice against NerdFontsSymbolsNerdFontBlank.sfd: once for SymbolsNerdFont-Regular.ttf and once with --mono for SymbolsNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf. It enables only glyph sets not already packaged by Debian.

The installed fonts are rebuilt from shipped source inputs. Font Logos is excluded because upstream license-audit.md lists it as Unlicensed and Debian's Nerd Fonts notes flag logo glyphs as likely non-distributable. Font Awesome, Material Design Icons, and Weather Icons are excluded because Debian packages them.

Companion font fallback
-----------------------

The package recommends fonts-font-awesome and fonts-materialdesignicons-legacy.
Its enabled 60-nerd-font-symbols.conf appends strongly bound Symbols Nerd Font,
FontAwesome, and Material Design Icons version 6/5 fallbacks to requests covered
by the upstream Nerd Font aliases (including monospace and Hack). The selected
text family stays ahead of these fallbacks; language matching no longer selects
unrelated private-use glyphs in fonts such as UnDotum first. The configuration
also covers explicit Symbols Nerd Font Mono requests.

Companion fonts provide only glyphs whose codepoints agree with Nerd Fonts:
FontAwesome supplies the legacy U+F000..U+F2FF icons, and Material Design Icons
version 6/5 supplies its available U+F0001 and higher icons. These packages do
not restore all icons from newer Nerd Fonts releases. In particular, newer Font
Awesome icons remapped into U+ED00..U+EFFF and Material Design icons absent from
the companion versions remain unavailable.

Do not add Weather Icons or the old Material Design Icons family to this
fallback list: Weather Icons uses U+F000..U+F0EB where Nerd Fonts uses
U+E300..U+E3EB, while the old Material Design font uses overlapping U+F000
codepoints instead of the supplementary private-use area. Fontconfig selects
families; it cannot remap codepoints. Recommending these incompatible fonts
would not restore the missing icons and could select the wrong glyphs.

Install the recommended packages unless deliberately accepting reduced icon
coverage. After an upgrade, restart applications that retain fontconfig state.

Regression checks
-----------------

In a disposable Debian unstable environment with the built package installed:

    apt-get install fontconfig fonts-hack fonts-unfonts-core \
        fonts-font-awesome fonts-materialdesignicons-legacy python3
    python3 debian/tests/fontconfig-fallback.py

The same checks are registered as a Debian autopkgtest. They exercise the four
icons in Debian bug #1149204, selected text and Powerline glyphs, bundled icons,
compatible Material Design icons, generic and explicit Mono requests, and
normal language fallback. The script ignores user-specific fontconfig files.
